[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 4: Second scenario: $ s + 2 $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s + 2 $ km/h, and the total time is 2.4 hours (including $ t $ minutes).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = 2.4 - \frac{t}{60}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 5: Let’s denote $ t $ in minutes, so $ t = \frac{t}{60} $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
