[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Geometry
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m A **rhombus** has:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - All sides equal in length.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Diagonals intersect at the **midpoint**, and they are **perpendicular**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - The diagonals bisect each other.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m In this case, the **diagonals intersect at the origin**, so the **center of the rhombus is at the origin**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let the diagonals be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $AC$ with midpoint at the origin
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $BD$ with midpoint at the origin
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So, the diagonals are **symmetric with respect to the origin**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let the coordinates of the vertices be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $A = (a, b)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $C = (-a, -b)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $B = (c, d)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $D = (-c, -d)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Then the diagonals are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $AC = (2a, 2b)$
