[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We are told:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - When Aya walks at speed $ s $, the walk takes 4 hours, including $ t $ minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - When she walks at speed $ s + 2 $, the walk takes 2 hours and 24 minutes, including $ t $ minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We are to find the total time taken when she walks at speed $ s + \frac{1}{2} $, again including $ t $ minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### **Step 2: Convert times to hours**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s convert all times to hours, so that we can work with consistent units.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - 4 hours = 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - 2 hours and 24 minutes = 2 + $ \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### **Step 3: Use the distance formula**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The distance $ d = 9 $ km is equal to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{distance} = \text{speed} \times \text{time}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 1: Speed = $ s $, time = 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = s \times 4 \Rightarrow s = \frac{9}{4} = 2.25 \text{ km/h}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 2: Speed = $ s + 2 $, time = 2.4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = (s + 2) \times 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Substitute $ s = 2.25 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = (2.25 + 2) \times 2.4 = 4.25 \times 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
