[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 2: Speed = $ s + 2 $, time = 144 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = (s + 2) \times \frac{144}{60} = (s + 2) \times 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Substitute $ s = 2.25 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = (2.25 + 2) \times 2.4 = 4.25 \times 2.4 = 10.2 \neq 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Still a contradiction. So we need to **redefine the total time**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### **Step 5: Let $ T $ be the total time in minutes**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s define:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ T $ = total time in minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ t $ = time spent in the coffee shop in minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Then:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 1: Speed = $ s $, time = $ T $, including $ t $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = s \times \frac{T}{60}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 2: Speed = $ s + 2 $, time = $ T $, including $ t $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 = (s + 2) \times \frac{T}{60}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So we have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
