[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 1: Set up equations based on the given information
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ t $ = time (in minutes) spent in the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ s $ = speed in km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ T $ = total time (in hours) for the walk, including the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m From the first scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - She walks 9 km at speed $ s $, taking $ \frac{9}{s} $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Total time = $ \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m From the second scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - She walks 9 km at speed $ s + 2 $, taking $ \frac{9}{s + 2} $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Total time = $ \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2 + \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 \tag{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now we have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 \tag{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Subtract equation (1) from equation (2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \left( \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} \right) - \left( \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} \right) = 2.4 - 4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Simplify:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} - \frac{9}{s} = -1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Factor out the 9:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 \left( \frac{1}{s + 2} - \frac{1}{s} \right) = -1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Compute the difference of fractions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{1}{s + 2} - \frac{1}{s} = \frac{s - (s + 2)}{s(s + 2)} = \frac{-2}{s(s + 2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9 \cdot \left( \frac{-2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = -1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{-18}{s(s + 2)} = -1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Multiply both sides by -1:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now solve for $ s $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s(s + 2) = \frac{18}{1.6} = 11.25
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s^2 + 2s - 11.25 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Solve the quadratic equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{4 + 4 \cdot 11.25}}{2} = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{49}}{2} = \frac{-2 \pm 7}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{5}{2} = 2.5 \quad \text{or} \quad s = \frac{-9}{2} = -4.5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Since speed cannot be negative, we take:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
