[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 1: Set up equations based on the given information
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ s $: speed in km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ t $: time in minutes spent in the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Total time for the walk (including coffee shop) = 4 hours = 240 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### First scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks at speed $ s $, takes 4 hours, including $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The time taken to walk 9 km is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time} = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Convert this to minutes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} \times 60 = \frac{540}{s} \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This time includes the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s} + t = 240 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Second scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks at speed $ s + 2 $, takes 2 hours and 24 minutes = 144 minutes, including $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Time taken to walk 9 km is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Convert to minutes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} \times 60 = \frac{540}{s + 2} \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This time includes the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} + t = 144 \tag{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Solve the system of equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We now have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 1. $ \frac{540}{s} + t = 240 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 2. $ \frac{540}{s + 2} + t = 144 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Subtract equation (2) from equation (1):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \left( \frac{540}{s} + t \right) - \left( \frac{540}{s + 2} + t \right) = 240 - 144
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s} - \frac{540}{s + 2} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Factor out 540:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 540 \left( \frac{1}{s} - \frac{1}{s + 2} \right) = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Compute the difference of fractions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{1}{s} - \frac{1}{s + 2} = \frac{(s + 2) - s}{s(s + 2)} = \frac{2}{s(s + 2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 540 \cdot \frac{2}{s(s + 2)} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{1080}{s(s + 2)} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Multiply both sides by $ s(s + 2) $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 1080 = 96s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Divide both sides by 48:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 22.5 = s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now solve the quadratic equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s^2 + 2s - 22.5 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Use the quadratic formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{2^2 - 4(1)(-22.5)}}{2(1)} = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{4 + 90}}{2} = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{94}}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Since speed cannot be negative, we take the positive root:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{-2 + \sqrt{94}}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now compute the numerical value of $ s $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \sqrt{94} \approx 9.7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s \approx \frac{-2 + 9.7}{2} = \frac{7.7}{2} = 3.85
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So $ s \approx 3.85 $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
