[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 3: Use the condition $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a key condition that will help us relate the sides of the triangle.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m There is a known formula in triangle geometry that relates the distance between the incenter and circumcenter:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m OI^2 = R(R - 2r)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a standard result:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
