[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 5: Use the condition $ \vec{IA} \perp \vec{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m From earlier:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ax + by = x^2 + y^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Also, we know that the incenter $ I $ lies at a distance $ r = 6 $ from the sides of the triangle, and the circumradius is $ R = 13 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We can use the formula for the distance from the incenter to the circumcenter:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr = 13^2 - 2 \cdot 13 \cdot 6 = 169 - 156 = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \Rightarrow OI = \sqrt{13}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So the distance between $ O $ and $ I $ is $ \sqrt{13} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We also know that $ \vec{IA} \perp \vec{OI} $, so the angle between $ \vec{IA} $ and $ \vec{OI} $ is 90°
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So the triangle has a specific configuration where the incenter lies on a circle of radius $ \sqrt{13} $, and the line $ IA $ is perpendicular to the line $ OI $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a very special triangle, and it is known in triangle geometry that such a triangle is **right-angled**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s assume $ \angle A = 90^\circ $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Then, the triangle is right-angled at $ A $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So, $ AB \perp AC $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ AB = c $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ AC = b $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ BC = a $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Then, the triangle is right-angled at $ A $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m a^2 = b^2 + c^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We are to find $ AB \cdot AC = bc $
