[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $AC: $A = (a, b), C = (-a, -b)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $BD: $B = (c, d), D = (-c, -d)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The diagonals intersect at the origin, so the origin is the midpoint of both diagonals.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Use the hyperbola equation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Since all points $A, B, C, D$ lie on the hyperbola, they satisfy the hyperbola equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{x^2}{20} - \frac{y^2}{24} = 1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
