[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Use the distance and time relationship
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The distance is 9 km, so we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### Case 1: Walking at $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m But the total time is 4 hours, including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Convert 4 hours to minutes: $ 4 \times 60 = 240 $ minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours} = 240 - t \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Convert $ \frac{9}{s} $ hours to minutes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} \times 60 = 240 - t
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s} = 240 - t \tag{1}
