[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Simplify the fraction
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s simplify the fraction:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9b + 7}{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We can perform polynomial division or rewrite the numerator in terms of the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 9b + 7 = 9(b + 7) - 63 + 7 = 9(b + 7) - 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9b + 7}{b + 7} = \frac{9(b + 7) - 56}{b + 7} = 9 - \frac{56}{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m For this to be an integer, $ \frac{56}{b + 7} $ must be an integer.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So, $ b + 7 $ must be a **divisor of 56**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
