[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 1: Use the given condition $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a key geometric condition. Let’s recall some properties:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ O $ is the **circumcenter** of $ \triangle ABC $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ I $ is the **incenter** of $ \triangle ABC $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ \overline{IA} $ is the line from the incenter to the vertex $ A $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ \overline{OI} $ is the line from the incenter to the circumcenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The condition $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $ implies that the incenter and circumcenter are **perpendicular** to the line from the incenter to the vertex $ A $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a **special configuration** of a triangle, and it is known that such a triangle has a specific relationship between its sides and the inradius and circumradius.
