[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 2: Use the formula for the distance between incenter and circumcenter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m The distance between the incenter $ I $ and the circumcenter $ O $ is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m This is a well-known formula in triangle geometry:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We are given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
