[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### Step 5: Use Symmetry and Parametrize the Hyperbola
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s parametrize the hyperbola:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{x^2}{20} - \frac{y^2}{24} = 1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We can use the standard parametrization:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m x = 2\sqrt{5} \sec \theta, \quad y = 2\sqrt{6} \tan \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m A = (2\sqrt{5} \sec \theta, 2\sqrt{6} \tan \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m B = (2\sqrt{5} \sec \phi, 2\sqrt{6} \tan \phi)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Since the diagonals are perpendicular and intersect at the origin, the vectors from the origin to the points are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $A = (x_1, y_1)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $B = (x_2, y_2)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $C = (-x_1, -y_1)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $D = (-x_2, -y_2)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So the diagonals are $AC$ and $BD$, and the vectors are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $\vec{AC} = (2x_1, 2y_1)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $\vec{BD} = (2x_2, 2y_2)$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Their dot product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \vec{AC} \cdot \vec{BD} = 4x_1x_2 + 4y_1y_2 = 0 \Rightarrow x_1x_2 + y_1y_2 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m x_1x_2 + y_1y_2 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now, since $A = (x_1, y_1)$ and $B = (x_2, y_2)$ lie on the hyperbola:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{x_1^2}{20} - \frac{y_1^2}{24} = 1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{x_2^2}{20} - \frac{y_2^2}{24} = 1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
