[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m [response] We are given a problem involving Aya's walking and coffee shop visit.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### **Given:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Aya walks **9 km** each morning.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - She stops at a coffee shop after her walk.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - She walks at a **constant speed of $ s $ km/h**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - The total time for the walk (including the coffee shop) is **4 hours**, and she spends **$ t $ minutes** in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - When she walks at **$ s + 2 $ km/h**, the total time is **2 hours and 24 minutes**, including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - We are to find the **time** it takes her to walk at **$ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h**, including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m ### **Step 1: Set up equations**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s define:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ s $: her walking speed in km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - $ t $: time in minutes she spends in the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Total time for the walk (including coffee shop) when she walks at $ s $ km/h: 4 hours = 240 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m - Total time for the walk (including coffee shop) when she walks at $ s + 2 $ km/h: 2 hours 24 minutes = 144 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s write the equations based on distance and time.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### **First scenario: Speed $ s $, time 240 minutes**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s $, and the total time is 240 minutes (including $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So, the time she spends walking is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time walking} = 240 - t \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time walking} = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours} = \frac{9}{s} \times 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s} \times 60 = 240 - t
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m #### **Second scenario: Speed $ s + 2 $, time 144 minutes**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s + 2 $, and the total time is 144 minutes (including $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So, the time she spends walking is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time walking} = 144 - t \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s + 2 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time walking} = \frac{9}{s + 2} \times 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} \times 60 = 144 - t
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now we have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 1. $ \frac{9 \times 60}{s} = 240 - t $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 2. $ \frac{9 \times 60}{s + 2} = 144 - t $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Let’s write them more clearly:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s} = 240 - t \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} = 144 - t \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now subtract equation (1) from equation (2):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} - \frac{540}{s} = (144 - t) - (240 - t)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} - \frac{540}{s} = 144 - t - 240 + t = -196
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now compute the left-hand side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} - \frac{540}{s} = 540 \left( \frac{1}{s + 2} - \frac{1}{s} \right) = 540 \left( \frac{s - (s + 2)}{s(s + 2)} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m = 540 \left( \frac{s - s - 2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = 540 \left( \frac{-2}{s(s + 2)} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 540 \left( \frac{-2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = -196
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Multiply both sides by $ -1 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 540 \left( \frac{2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = 196
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now solve for $ s $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{1080}{s(s + 2)} = 196
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Multiply both sides by $ s(s + 2) $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 1080 = 196s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Expand the right-hand side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 1080 = 196s^2 + 392s
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Bring all terms to one side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 196s^2 + 392s - 1080 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Divide through by 4 to simplify:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 49s^2 + 98s - 270 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{-98 \pm \sqrt{98^2 - 4 \cdot 49 \cdot (-270)}}{2 \cdot 49}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Compute the discriminant:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 98^2 = 9604
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 4 \cdot 49 \cdot 270 = 1260
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Discriminant} = 9604 + 1260 = 1264
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s = \frac{-98 \pm \sqrt{1264}}{98}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now compute $ \sqrt{1264} $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \sqrt{1264} = \sqrt{16 \cdot 79} = 4\sqrt{79} \approx 4 \cdot 8.89 = 35.56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s \approx \frac{-98 \pm 35.56}{98}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We take the positive root:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s \approx \frac{-98 + 35.56}{98} \approx 0.361
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s \approx 0.361 \text{ km/h}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now plug this back into one of the original equations to find $ t $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Use equation (1):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{s} = 240 - t
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \frac{540}{0.361} \approx 149.56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m t \approx 240 - 149.56 = 140.44 \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m Now we are asked to find the time it takes her to walk at $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h, including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m \text{Time} = \frac{9}{s + \frac{1}{2}} \times 60 \text{ minutes}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m We already have $ s \approx 0.361 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m s + \frac{1}{2} \approx 0.361 + 0.5 = 0.861
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13660)[0m So:
